{
  "number": 22,
  "chapter": "Luke 22",
  "source": "https://berean.bible/downloads.htm",
  "translation": "Berean Standard Bible (BSB)",
  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": 1,
      "text": "Now the Feast of Unleavened Bread, called the Passover, was approaching,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 2,
      "text": "and the chief priests and scribes were looking for a way to put Jesus to death, for they feared the people."
    },
    {
      "verse": 3,
      "text": "Then Satan entered Judas Iscariot, who was one of the Twelve."
    },
    {
      "verse": 4,
      "text": "And Judas went to discuss with the chief priests and temple officers how he might betray Jesus to them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 5,
      "text": "They were delighted and agreed to give him money."
    },
    {
      "verse": 6,
      "text": "Judas consented, and began to look for an opportunity to betray Jesus to them in the absence of a crowd."
    },
    {
      "verse": 7,
      "text": "Then came the day of Unleavened Bread on which the Passover lamb was to be sacrificed."
    },
    {
      "verse": 8,
      "text": "Jesus sent Peter and John, saying, “Go and make preparations for us to eat the Passover.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 9,
      "text": "“Where do You want us to prepare it?” they asked."
    },
    {
      "verse": 10,
      "text": "He answered, “When you enter the city, a man carrying a jug of water will meet you. Follow him to the house he enters,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 11,
      "text": "and say to the owner of that house, ‘The Teacher asks: Where is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’"
    },
    {
      "verse": 12,
      "text": "And he will show you a large upper room, already furnished. Make preparations there.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 13,
      "text": "So they went and found it just as Jesus had told them. And they prepared the Passover."
    },
    {
      "verse": 14,
      "text": "When the hour had come, Jesus reclined at the table with His apostles."
    },
    {
      "verse": 15,
      "text": "And He said to them, “I have eagerly desired to eat this Passover with you before My suffering."
    },
    {
      "verse": 16,
      "text": "For I tell you that I will not eat it again until it is fulfilled in the kingdom of God.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 17,
      "text": "After taking the cup, He gave thanks and said, “Take this and divide it among yourselves."
    },
    {
      "verse": 18,
      "text": "For I tell you that I will not drink of the fruit of the vine from now on until the kingdom of God comes.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 19,
      "text": "And He took the bread, gave thanks and broke it, and gave it to them, saying, “This is My body, given for you; do this in remembrance of Me.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 20,
      "text": "In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new covenant in My blood, which is poured out for you."
    },
    {
      "verse": 21,
      "text": "Look! The hand of My betrayer is with Mine on the table."
    },
    {
      "verse": 22,
      "text": "Indeed, the Son of Man will go as it has been determined, but woe to that man who betrays Him.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 23,
      "text": "Then they began to question among themselves which of them was going to do this."
    },
    {
      "verse": 24,
      "text": "A dispute also arose among the disciples as to which of them should be considered the greatest."
    },
    {
      "verse": 25,
      "text": "So Jesus declared, “The kings of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those in authority over them call themselves benefactors."
    },
    {
      "verse": 26,
      "text": "But you shall not be like them. Instead, the greatest among you should be like the youngest, and the one who leads like the one who serves."
    },
    {
      "verse": 27,
      "text": "For who is greater, the one who reclines at the table or the one who serves? Is it not the one who reclines? But I am among you as one who serves."
    },
    {
      "verse": 28,
      "text": "You are the ones who have stood by Me in My trials."
    },
    {
      "verse": 29,
      "text": "And I bestow on you a kingdom, just as My Father has bestowed one on Me,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 30,
      "text": "so that you may eat and drink at My table in My kingdom and sit on thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel."
    },
    {
      "verse": 31,
      "text": "Simon, Simon, Satan has asked to sift all of you like wheat."
    },
    {
      "verse": 32,
      "text": "But I have prayed for you, Simon, that your faith will not fail. And when you have turned back, strengthen your brothers.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 33,
      "text": "“Lord,” said Peter, “I am ready to go with You even to prison and to death.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 34,
      "text": "But Jesus replied, “I tell you, Peter, the rooster will not crow today until you have denied three times that you know Me.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 35,
      "text": "Then Jesus asked them, “When I sent you out without purse or bag or sandals, did you lack anything?” “Nothing,” they answered."
    },
    {
      "verse": 36,
      "text": "“Now, however,” He told them, “the one with a purse should take it, and likewise a bag; and the one without a sword should sell his cloak and buy one."
    },
    {
      "verse": 37,
      "text": "For I tell you that this Scripture must be fulfilled in Me: ‘And He was numbered with the transgressors.’ For what is written about Me is reaching its fulfillment.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 38,
      "text": "So they said, “Look, Lord, here are two swords.” “That is enough,” He answered."
    },
    {
      "verse": 39,
      "text": "Jesus went out as usual to the Mount of Olives, and the disciples followed Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 40,
      "text": "When He came to the place, He told them, “Pray that you will not enter into temptation.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 41,
      "text": "And He withdrew about a stone’s throw beyond them, where He knelt down and prayed,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 42,
      "text": "“Father, if You are willing, take this cup from Me. Yet not My will, but Yours be done.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 43,
      "text": "Then an angel from heaven appeared to Him and strengthened Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 44,
      "text": "And in His anguish, He prayed more earnestly, and His sweat became like drops of blood falling to the ground."
    },
    {
      "verse": 45,
      "text": "When Jesus rose from prayer and returned to the disciples, He found them asleep, exhausted from sorrow."
    },
    {
      "verse": 46,
      "text": "“Why are you sleeping?” He asked. “Get up and pray so that you will not enter into temptation.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 47,
      "text": "While He was still speaking, a crowd arrived, led by the man called Judas, one of the Twelve. He approached Jesus to kiss Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 48,
      "text": "But Jesus asked him, “Judas, are you betraying the Son of Man with a kiss?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 49,
      "text": "Those around Jesus saw what was about to happen and said, “Lord, should we strike with our swords?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 50,
      "text": "And one of them struck the servant of the high priest, cutting off his right ear."
    },
    {
      "verse": 51,
      "text": "But Jesus answered, “No more of this!” And He touched the man’s ear and healed him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 52,
      "text": "Then Jesus said to the chief priests, temple officers, and elders who had come for Him, “Have you come out with swords and clubs as you would against an outlaw?"
    },
    {
      "verse": 53,
      "text": "Every day I was with you in the temple courts, and you did not lay a hand on Me. But this hour belongs to you and to the power of darkness.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 54,
      "text": "Then they seized Jesus, led Him away, and took Him into the house of the high priest. And Peter followed at a distance."
    },
    {
      "verse": 55,
      "text": "When those present had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and sat down together, Peter sat down among them."
    },
    {
      "verse": 56,
      "text": "A servant girl saw him seated in the firelight and looked intently at him. “This man also was with Him,” she said."
    },
    {
      "verse": 57,
      "text": "But Peter denied it. “Woman, I do not know Him,” he said."
    },
    {
      "verse": 58,
      "text": "A short time later, someone else saw him and said, “You also are one of them.” But Peter said, “Man, I am not.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 59,
      "text": "About an hour later, another man insisted, “Certainly this man was with Him, for he too is a Galilean.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 60,
      "text": "“Man, I do not know what you are talking about,” Peter replied. And immediately, while he was still speaking, the rooster crowed."
    },
    {
      "verse": 61,
      "text": "And the Lord turned and looked at Peter. Then Peter remembered the word that the Lord had spoken to him: “Before the rooster crows today, you will deny Me three times.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 62,
      "text": "And he went outside and wept bitterly."
    },
    {
      "verse": 63,
      "text": "The men who were holding Jesus began to mock Him and beat Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 64,
      "text": "They blindfolded Him and kept demanding, “Prophesy! Who hit You?”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 65,
      "text": "And they said many other blasphemous things against Him."
    },
    {
      "verse": 66,
      "text": "At daybreak the council of the elders of the people, both the chief priests and scribes, met together. They led Jesus into their Sanhedrin and said,"
    },
    {
      "verse": 67,
      "text": "“If You are the Christ, tell us.” Jesus answered, “If I tell you, you will not believe."
    },
    {
      "verse": 68,
      "text": "And if I ask you a question, you will not answer."
    },
    {
      "verse": 69,
      "text": "But from now on the Son of Man will be seated at the right hand of the power of God.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 70,
      "text": "So they all asked, “Are You then the Son of God?” He replied, “You say that I am.”"
    },
    {
      "verse": 71,
      "text": "“Why do we need any more testimony?” they declared. “We have heard it for ourselves from His own lips.”"
    }
  ],
